Southern Market Square~
   The southern edge of the great Market Square, and the press of people
here is a weight on the chest. Stalls sell rope, lamp oil, salt, second-hand
boots taken off the dead. Hawkers cry prices that rise every week. The
square continues north, east and west, and the Medina leads off south.
