#5410
The Common Square~
   Once a grassy field, the Common Square is trodden to bare earth by the
refugees who sleep here when the city has no other room for them. Smoke from
cook-fires hangs low. The river can be heard to the south, beyond the bridge
and the South Gate. Isvar Drive runs east and west along the water, and the
Medina leads north.
